      "content": [
        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "No. A 10% month-over-month sales decline alone doesn’t establish that the campaign failed.\n\nYou’d need to consider:\n\n- **Campaign objective and KPIs:** awareness, leads, conversions, revenue, or profit\n- **Seasonality and market trends**\n- **Changes in price, inventory, distribution, or competitors**\n- **Customer segments exposed to the campaign**\n- **Performance versus a control group or credible baseline**\n- **Campaign cost and incremental return**\n\nFor example, sales might have fallen 10% overall but would have fallen 20% without the campaign. Assess **incremental lift and ROI**, ideally through an A/B test or matched control, before drawing a conclusion."
        }
      ]
    },
